<section id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Defense: PromptGuard</h5>

<div id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We ran a challenge in which the model <span id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">PromptGuard-2 86M</span> was used as a defense. The defended challenge used user task 0 and injection task 5 from the SLACK suite in AgentDojo. Our PromptGuard defense was setup as a <span id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">PromptInjectionDetector</span> in the AgentDojo package, but due to hardware constraints we hosted the model on a HuggingFace inference endpoint. The model was not quantized or altered in any way.</p>
</div>
